<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan aluminium imports up 16.4 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan aluminium imports up 16.4 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined aluminium imports rose to 230,552 tonnes in January, up 16.4 percent from 198,080 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry statistics released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Jan 96	    Dec 96	Jan 95</p>
<p> Total	  230,552	   211,553     198,080</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Brazil	  24,657	    33,197	20,633</p>
<p> Russia	  38,589	    39,892	30,720</p>
<p> Australia     39,896	    26,477	38,028</p>
<p> U.S.	    10,232	    11,268	18,727</p>
<p>Refined aluminium imports in 1996 were 2,758,853 tonnes, off 1.6 percent from 2,802,781 tonnes from the year before.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
